<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/11th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle on the Nemiga River</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1067</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle on the Nemiga River was fought on 3 March 1067 near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/minsk">Minsk</a> between Prince <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vseslav-of-polotsk">Vseslav of Polotsk</a> and the three sons of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yaroslav-the-wise">Yaroslav the Wise</a>, Iziaslav, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sviatoslav-i-of-kiev">Sviatoslav</a> and Vsevolod. The Yaroslavichi, who had sacked Minsk, defeated Vseslav and later seized him by treachery. The battle, the first event in which Minsk is recorded, is described in the Tale of Igor's Campaign.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-on-the-nemiga-river.jpg" alt="Battle on the Nemiga River" width="320" height="164" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown artistUnknown artist · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Battle_on_Nemiga_02.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
